From 34060a0d9d758fd15ad595cafd1b82ac1ee8966b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 23:00:15 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Derive P05 field sizes from the authenticated transaction

Caller hints for UTXOPATH, UTXOOUTPUT, OUTPUTPATH and OUTPUTRECORD can
be omitted when an execution context is present. The charge uses the
serialized size of that field. A hint below the field still fails. A
larger hint is kept and only overcharges. With no context, an absent
hint still uses MAX_ELEMENT_BYTES.

This does not parse, connect, or accept a V2 block.
